        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 19.44,
          "end": 21.42,
          "en": "and reply something to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 21.42,
          "end": 23.79,
          "en": "And of course in Java we don't build the front end, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 23.79,
          "end": 27.45,
          "en": "The front end is built using HTML, CSS, JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 27.45,
          "end": 29.82,
          "en": "So you can use HTML, CSS and Vanilla JS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 29.82,
          "end": 30.817,
          "en": "to bring the front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 30.817,
          "end": 33.03,
          "en": "Or you can use something called React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 33.03,
          "end": 34.71,
          "en": "to build your front end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 34.71,
          "end": 37.35,
          "en": "Or you can also use a mobile application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 37.35,
          "end": 40.71,
          "en": "Or maybe there is some other server using your server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 40.71,
          "end": 42,
          "en": "to get some data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 42,
          "end": 45.45,
          "en": "Ultimately, your server is basically giving some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 45.45,
          "end": 47.34,
          "en": "back to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 47.34,
          "end": 48.173,
          "en": "Now the thing is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 48.173,
          "end": 50.04,
          "en": "if we talk about building a web application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 50.04,
          "end": 52.38,
          "en": "of course we have done that with the help of Servlet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 52.38,
          "end": 56.28,
          "en": "Now think about this. What if you want to return a data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 56.28,
          "end": 58.589,
          "en": "So it's very simple, you can say, hey Servlet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 58.589,
          "end": 60.54,
          "en": "to get some data from the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 60.54,
          "end": 63.27,
          "en": "So, Servlet will talk to database and get your data back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 63.27,
          "end": 65.4,
          "en": "and say, okay, this is your data, take it back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 65.4,
          "end": 68.13,
          "en": "Now if you just want return data, it's very simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 68.13,
          "end": 70.44,
          "en": "But then we know that if you want your client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 70.44,
          "end": 72.33,
          "en": "to see some data on a browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 72.33,
          "end": 74.25,
          "en": "you cannot simply send a data, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 74.25,
          "end": 75.12,
          "en": "That's boring.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 75.12,
          "end": 76.35,
          "en": "You want to make it interesting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 76.35,
          "end": 79.2,
          "en": "and that's why you will use a beautiful front end, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 79.2,
          "end": 80.46000000000001,
          "en": "Now, the question arise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 80.46000000000001,
          "end": 84.12,
          "en": "if you want to return a front end from your Servlet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 84.12,
          "end": 88.05,
          "en": "basically you have to write STML tags inside Java, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 88.05,
          "end": 90.45,
          "en": "And then we have done that in the last video.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 90.45,
          "end": 91.68,
          "en": "And that's what the problem starts, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 91.68,
          "end": 94.97999999999999,
          "en": "If you start adding STML content inside the Java code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 94.97999999999999,
          "end": 96.42,
          "en": "what if it becomes bulky?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 99.6,
          "en": "And that's where you have to find a solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 99.6,
          "end": 102.18,
          "en": "And that solution is JSP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 102.18,
          "end": 105.36,
          "en": "Now again, in Java we have multiple view technologies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 105.36,
          "end": 107.94,
          "en": "That's why we call them as view technologies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 107.94,
          "end": 110.52000000000001,
          "en": "because we create them to show to the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 110.52000000000001,
          "end": 114,
          "en": "So in Servlet, basically you write STML inside Java.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 114,
          "end": 115.25999999999999,
          "en": "But can we do something like this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 115.25999999999999,
          "end": 118.83,
          "en": "Can we write HTML page, the entire page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 118.83,
          "end": 121.32,
          "en": "and put the Java code in between?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 121.32,
          "end": 122.43,
          "en": "Yes, that's possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 122.43,
          "end": 125.73,
          "en": "And that's where we have something called JSP,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 125.73,
          "end": 127.98,
          "en": "which stands for Java Server Pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 127.98,
          "end": 129.96,
          "en": "And this is not the only view technology.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 129.96,
          "end": 132.33,
          "en": "There are multiple, you can see the list here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 132.33,
          "end": 133.23,
          "en": "I mean not the complete list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 133.23,
          "end": 134.97,
          "en": "but then we have multiple there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 134.97,
          "end": 137.91,
          "en": "So we can use JSP to create the view technology.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 137.91,
          "end": 139.5,
          "en": "Now coming talking about these two things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 139.5,
          "end": 141.57,
          "en": "we got Servlet and we got JSP.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 141.57,
          "end": 143.43,
          "en": "Now Servlet is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 143.43,
          "end": 145.35,
          "en": "to accept the request from the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 145.35,
          "end": 148.14,
          "en": "and JSP is responsible to create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 148.14,
          "end": 149.79,
          "en": "that beautiful page which you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 149.79,
          "end": 153,
          "en": "That means you can do your processing in Servlet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 153,
          "end": 154.2,
          "en": "I mean not just processing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 154.2,
          "end": 156.21,
          "en": "you can accept the request from the Servlet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 156.21,
          "end": 157.92000000000002,
          "en": "You can do the processing there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 157.92000000000002,
          "end": 160.2,
          "en": "and then once you get your data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 160.2,
          "end": 163.59,
          "en": "just send that data to JSP page and JSP will send that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 163.59,
          "end": 165.42000000000002,
          "en": "to the client with the HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 165.42000000000002,
          "end": 167.49,
          "en": "Okay?, so if we have to use both at the same time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 167.49,
          "end": 169.5,
          "en": "Can we do that? Yes we can.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 169.5,
          "end": 171.12,
          "en": "So basically in the same application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 171.12,
          "end": 174.6,
          "en": "we can use Servlet and JSP as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 174.6,
          "end": 176.34,
          "en": "Again, once we start with Spring Boot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 176.34,
          "end": 177.93,
          "en": "I will show you how JSP looks like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 177.93,
          "end": 181.86,
          "en": "But imagine JSP page as a page which has HTML tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 181.86,
          "end": 183.03,
          "en": "but somewhere in between",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 183.03,
          "end": 185.34,
          "en": "you can actually write the Java code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 185.34,
          "end": 186.9,
          "en": "Okay, now, is it complete?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 186.9,
          "end": 188.46,
          "en": "See, the thing is when you talk about Java,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 188.46,
          "end": 190.59,
          "en": "Java is object oriented, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 190.59,
          "end": 192.12,
          "en": "So whatever data you want to represent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 192.12,
          "end": 193.08,
          "en": "you should be representing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 193.08,
          "end": 194.85,
          "en": "with the help of object format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 194.85,
          "end": 196.95,
          "en": "That means, let's say if a client says,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 196.95,
          "end": 199.41,
          "en": "hey, you know I want a student data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 199.41,
          "end": 200.82,
          "en": "Now, in the table, in the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 200.82,
          "end": 202.5,
          "en": "you do have a student data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 202.5,
          "end": 205.26,
          "en": "Now, when you get that data in your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 205.26,
          "end": 208.14,
          "en": "don't just keep that data in simple variables.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 208.14,
          "end": 209.97,
          "en": "You have to save that in an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 209.97,
          "end": 211.41,
          "en": "That means basically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 211.41,
          "end": 213.51,
          "en": "we have to use these three technologies now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 213.51,
          "end": 216.3,
          "en": "Servlet, to accept the request from the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 216.3,
          "end": 218.52,
          "en": "JSP, to show it to the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 218.52,
          "end": 223.14,
          "en": "and this data, which is your object, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 223.14,
          "end": 226.38,
          "en": "Now this is where we get a term called MVC.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 226.38,
          "end": 228.9,
          "en": "Now this is not specific to Java,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 228.9,
          "end": 230.85,
          "en": "whenever you talk about web applications",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 230.85,
          "end": 233.1,
          "en": "we use this pattern, which is called MVC,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 233.1,
          "end": 236.01,
          "en": "which stands for Model View Controller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 236.01,
          "end": 237.57,
          "en": "So what we basically do is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 237.57,
          "end": 239.52,
          "en": "let's say if you're building a web application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 239.52,
          "end": 241.11,
          "en": "and if a client says, hey, you know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 241.11,
          "end": 243.72,
          "en": "I want to add two numbers, or maybe a client says,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 243.72,
          "end": 245.07,
          "en": "I have a ID here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 245.07,
          "end": 246.57,
          "en": "Let's say ID is 101.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 246.57,
          "end": 249.57,
          "en": "I want to get the details of this particular person",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 249.57,
          "end": 250.95,
          "en": "with an ID 101.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 250.95,
          "end": 253.08,
          "en": "Person means student or someone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 253.08,
          "end": 255.63,
          "en": "Now in this case, when a client sends a request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 255.63,
          "end": 258.12,
          "en": "the request goes to the controller.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 258.12,
          "end": 261.84,
          "en": "Now this controller is responsible to accept the request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 261.84,
          "end": 265.53,
          "en": "and then depend upon what type of request you get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 265.53,
          "end": 267.51,
          "en": "if it says, okay, I want some data from database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 267.51,
          "end": 270.27,
          "en": "it will talk to database, get the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 270.27,
          "end": 272.76,
          "en": "and maybe you wanted some extra processing or something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 272.76,
          "end": 274.8,
          "en": "or you want to represent this data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 274.8,
          "end": 276.6,
          "en": "you will be using an object there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 276.6,
          "end": 278.52,
          "en": "And that's why we call them as model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 278.52,
          "end": 281.04,
          "en": "So your object in which you have your data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 281.04,
          "end": 282.3,
          "en": "is called a model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 282.3,
          "end": 285.93,
          "en": "And then when you want to send this data, the model object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 285.93,
          "end": 287.397,
          "en": "which has a certain data to the client",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 287.397,
          "end": 290.07,
          "en": "to can't say send directly the model object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 290.07,
          "end": 291.3,
          "en": "What you do is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 291.3,
          "end": 295.08,
          "en": "a controller will send this data to our view technology.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 295.08,
          "end": 297.27,
          "en": "So when I say data, I'm talking about the model object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 297.27,
          "end": 299.90999999999997,
          "en": "So this model object goes from the controller",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 299.90999999999997,
          "end": 300.9,
          "en": "to the view technology,",
